{
  "dom_id": "step-e14173",
  "name": "Example: Identifying the Range of a Piecewise Function",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194340/assets/a277f71617ce2dceae7ee97017655c4c27e57a9bb22020995905760e53bf7720.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?",
  "worked_solution": "We find the ranges of the individual pieces, and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [-2,1]$ is $[-2,2].$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (1,5)$ is $(1,3].$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $[-2,2] \\cup (1,3] = [-2,3].$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
